  "public_messages": [
    "I\u2019ll inspect BRIEF.md, the current source, and the supplied test first. Then I\u2019ll implement the API, add focused verification, and update the project notes with what was actually checked.",
    "The workspace has a supplied SQLite helper and test, but no API implementation yet. I\u2019ll preserve those files and use database transactions to coordinate claims and idempotency across processes.",
    "The server now builds and the supplied driver test passes. I\u2019m adding API tests for the transaction and lease cases, then I\u2019ll verify behavior across two processes and a restart.",
    "The API tests now pass after a small test-file fix. They cover duplicate submissions, tenant isolation, stale tokens, deadline equality, heartbeat, completion replay, and batch validation. Next I\u2019m checking the built binary against a shared database and a restart.",
    "The first two-process check found a startup race: one server could get `SQLITE_BUSY` while both initialized the schema. I\u2019m adding bounded retries around initialization, then I\u2019ll rerun the process check.",
    "The two-process check now passes: both servers open the same file, replay resolves to one job, and the job remains after a SIGKILL and restart. I also added a shared-database claim test. I\u2019m tightening request validation before the final verification pass.",
    "Final checks are passing so far. I also made writes reassert `synchronous=FULL` on their active SQLite connection, so durability settings hold if `database/sql` replaces a connection. I\u2019ll run the tests and build once more after that change, then record the exact results.",
    "Implemented the QueueForge backend in [service.go](<WORKSPACE>/internal/queueforge/service.go) and the [server entry point](<WORKSPACE>/cmd/server/main.go). It includes transactional SQLite writes, tenant isolation, idempotent single and batch submission, lease fencing, lifecycle operations, stats, and the optional test clock. I added focused [tests](<WORKSPACE>/internal/queueforge/service_test.go), a [README](<WORKSPACE>/README.md), and updated [PROJECT_NOTES.md](<WORKSPACE>/PROJECT_NOTES.md).\n\n**Verified:** the build, `go test ./...`, and `go test -race ./...` pass. A loopback check confirmed that two server processes share one database, an idempotent replay returns the same job, and the job remains after SIGKILL and restart. That check exposed a concurrent startup lock; bounded initialization retries fixed it. The supplied driver files and exact `go.mod`/`go.sum` are unchanged. No commit was made.\n\nThe two-process check did not exercise simultaneous cross-process claims; the shared-database claim test used two service instances. Owned test processes were stopped."
  ],
